 A campaign billboard in Tel Aviv yesterday. Photo: Jack Guez/AFP via Getty Images 🇮🇱 High voter turnout in today's Israeli elections — the most in 53 years — will likely push several of the parties in Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's bloc below the electoral threshold. That will make it harder for Netanyahu to reach a 61-seat majority. More from Barak Ravid , reporting from Tel Aviv. 🚔 Two men were charged with national security offenses over a suspected plot against RAF Fairford, a U.S.-run military air base in England. Go deeper . 👨‍⚕️ People magazine named "The Pitt" star Noah Wyle as the 2026 Sexiest Man Alive. "I thought that sounded like a prank — just not in a million years did I think that this would be an honor bestowed on me," he said. Go deeper . 
 
